22 15.42 11.57 15.65C10.93 15.88 10.23 16 9.5 16ZM9.5 14C10.75 14 11.81 13.56 12.69 12.69C13.56 11.81 14 10.75 14 9.5C14 8.25 13.56 7.19 12.69 6.31C11.81 5.44 10.75 5 9.5 5C8.25 5 7.19 5.44 6.31 6.31C5.44 7.19 5 8.25 5 9.5C5 10.75 5.44 11.81 6.31 12.69C7.19 13.56 8.25 14 9.5 14Z" fill="#006BAA"/> </svg></div></div></button></div><!----></div></div></div></div></div><div class="faqs__inner" data-v-b67004cf><section class="faqs__wrapper" data-v-b67004cf><div class="faqs__content" data-v-b67004cf><div class="faqs__inner-slices" data-v-b67004cf><div data-v-b67004cf><!--[--><section id="can-i-upload-multiple-parcels-using-a-csv-file?" class="section-wrapper rich-text" index="0" data-v-92714c58 data-v-ebc71926><div class="section-wrapper__container" data-v-ebc71926><!--[--><!--[--><h1><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Can I upload multiple parcels using a CSV file?<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--]--><!--]--></h1><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Yes, you can upload parcel details in a CSV file using a Microsoft Excel spreadsheet template that we’ve created so that all the required details match up at our end, it just makes it a bit easier for you when you come to upload them.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->To upload a CSV file, you will need to<!--]--><!--]--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><a href="/sign-in" rel="noreferrer"><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->log in to your Evri account<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></a><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> and select ‘Bulk import’, which gives you the option to search your computer or storage drives for the CSV file to upload. If this is the first time you’ve imported a CSV file, we may ask you to provide some default information. This will help speed up how quickly imports can be made in future.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Once you’ve imported your CSV file, it’s simply a case of deciding whether you want to add the parcels straight to the basket, or view and edit your import first.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><!--]--><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></div></div></div><div class="faqs-right-coumn" data-v-b67004cf><!----></div></section><div class="faqs-accordion__container" data-v-b67004cf data-v-538ce356><section class="faqs-accordion" data-v-538ce356><!--[--><div class="e-accordion-row" data-test-id="faq-links-accordion-row-0" data-v-538ce356 data-v-fe7dd93b><button id="accordion-button-faq-links-0" type="button" aria-controls="accordion-content-faq-links-0" aria-expanded="false" class="e-accordion-row__header" data-test-id="faq-links-accordion-row-0-header" data-v-fe7dd93b><!--[--><!----><span class="e-accordion-row__header-text" data-test-id="faq-links-accordion-row-0-header-text" data-v-fe7dd93b>Account</span><!--]--><div class="e-icon e-accordion-row__chevron" aria-hidden="true" data-icon="chevron_down" data-test-id="chevron_down" data-v-fe7dd93b data-v-d0e20aa0><svg height="24" width="24" style="line-height:24px" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><title>chevron down</title> <g> <path d="M11.62 14.91C11.51 14.87 11.4 14.8 11.3 14.7L6.7 10.1C6.52 9.92 6.42 9.68 6.42 9.4C6.42 9.12 6.52 8.88 6.7 8.7C6.88 8.52 7.12 8.43 7.4 8.43C7.68 8.43 7.92 8.52 8.1 8.7L12 12.6L15.9 8.7C16.08 8.52 16.32 8.43 16.6 8.43C16.88 8.43 17.12 8.52 17.3 8.7C17.48 8.88 17.57 9.12 17.57 9.4C17.57 9.68 17.48 9.92 17.3 10.1L12.7 14.7C12.6 14.8 12.49 14.87 12.37 14.91C12.26 14.95 12.13 14.97 12 14.97C11.87 14.97 11.74 14.95 11.62 14.91Z" fill="#006BAA"/> </g> </svg></div></button><section id="accordion-content-faq-links-0" aria-labelledby="accordion-button-faq-links-0" class="e-accordion-row__content" data-test-id="faq-links-accordion-row-0-body-text" style="display:none;" data-v-fe7dd93b><div class="e-accordion-row__body" data-v-fe7d